<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:22:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4631c5cadfe6289f9ba37643bb13348b1ca2a4f12990572fd7b4a71f283b2e0c</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:22:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin businesswoman charged with spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ace196c51b400d47718e311034f5bd230160ba3b41c7883f21bab816fe8ea4e8</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T11:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-businesswoman-charged-with-spying-for-russia/a-79258004--e5381277f598.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-businesswoman-charged-with-spying-for-russia/a-79258004?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the Berlin marketing executive used her political and military contacts to help a Russian intelligence officer gain access to influential circles and seek information on German defense policy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Merz's CDU comes out on top in Lower Saxony polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce3001a3077799b48b00593f8e1b9d729d78f02438fead8db212fcf506b60cb</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724--04c4d8ef8565.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats have emerged as the strongest party following local elections in the state of Lower Saxony. The vote was closely watched as an indicator of the strength of the far-right AfD, which came in third.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6249b34648d5e0d6b92e96693b7235a86d923e34517cb400e4a28816dae68ad0</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: AfD questions German aid, Berlin remains committed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:290e2e045d8c3471e64a8091918b24fe631caff2d80105ccc5b91f1efc341025</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-afd-questions-german-aid-berlin-remains-committed/a-79257524--cdb3e9ec23f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-afd-questions-german-aid-berlin-remains-committed/a-79257524?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emboldened by its win in Saxony-Anhalt, the far-right Alternative for Germany wants the government to change its Ukraine and Russia policies. Berlin is staying the course, but support is fading — especially in the east.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f17de51251260307333575376a4c495404ddbc6714bae64e99dd8fdb83f844d</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU ahead in Lower Saxony local election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4772622ca95de400465a3f0f13a746a896cfeeb94d9385e46bac139a1f40bfaa</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T00:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427--aff1c7ebec22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The CDU is on course to win in municipal polls in the northwestern state of Lower Saxony that were seen as a gauge of support for the far-right AfD party.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
